A command palette card: a search field with a ⌘K hint, grouped commands with icons and keyboard shortcuts, and a
footer of key hints. A **block** composed from [Input](<%= page_path(:input) %>), Kbd,
[Navigation](<%= page_path(:navigation) %>) and Icon, as on the [Appica homepage](https://appica.dev/ui).

<%= embed AppicaUI::Blocks::CommandMenuPreview, :default %>

## Usage

```ruby
CommandMenu do
  CommandGroup(label: "Suggestions") do
    CommandItem(icon: :layout_dashboard, shortcut: %w[G D], href: dashboard_path) { "Open dashboard" }
    CommandItem(icon: :user_plus, shortcut: %w[⌘ I], value: "invite") { "Invite teammates" }
  end
  CommandGroup(label: "Actions") do
    CommandItem(icon: :rocket, shortcut: %w[⇧ D], value: "deploy") { "Deploy to production" }
  end
end
```

- Typing filters the commands by their label (ignoring case and accents); groups with no match hide, and
  "No matching commands" shows when nothing is left.
- ↑ / ↓ move the highlight (wrapping around), ↵ runs the highlighted command, Escape clears the search. Hovering
  highlights too.
- ⌘K / Ctrl+K focuses the search from anywhere on the page (`hotkey:` changes the key, `hotkey: nil` turns it off;
  `hotkey_hint:` is the Kbd shown in the field).
- A command with `href:` is a link; one without is a button. Running either emits
  `appica-ui--blocks--command-menu:select` with `{ value, label }` - cancel it to keep a link from being followed.

```js
document.addEventListener("appica-ui--blocks--command-menu:select", ({ detail }) => {
  if (detail.value === "dark-mode") document.documentElement.classList.toggle("dark")
})
```

`shortcut:` only displays the keys - bind them in your app if they should work globally.

## Localization

`command_menu.locales.yml` holds the placeholder, labels, empty message and key hints (English, Czech, German,
Arabic).

